            "review_title": "Review at El Toro - Home for Steaks & Wines",
            "review_text": "Amy Minh Hạnh C\n1 contribution\n0\nNot enough stars to leave an honest review\nJun 2026 • Family\nI’ve been to a lot of steakhouses in my life… El Toro is hands down the best, and I know that is a bold statement . \n\nThe first time I went was in March and I went on a date night and reserved via Instagram with their employee Teddy, who’s kindness, way of words and welcoming invite made us soo excited. Our first time was so amazing to discover the insane taste of their menu and unique, classy and care of each flavor and dish. We got the ribeye & everything that came with it like the lamb taretare (11/10) & the bone marrow (10/10 my husband ate most of it) and the spaghetti bolognese with steak! Superb ! My husband is French so we ordered it “rare” and they cooked it PERFECTLY! Idk how we ate desert but we did and it was incredible ! put aside the amazing food, i dont know if I have ever met & has been taken care of by better… i dont even want to call them employees of the restaurant because they make you feel like family, and that you belong and dont want to leave… We were so well taken care of, and even got to meet the whole kitchen & got to thank everyone.\n\nSomehow even though our first time was the best, our second time was better!!!!!! I went back for a late birthday dinner and we tried their porter steak AND we got the ribyeye again, a lot of the same appetisers and sides but got the shrimp bisque and it was wonderful! \nWe ordered more drinks and they had EVERYTHING we desired from Rosé to red wine, to Japanese Whisky! \n\nThe experience felt like dinner with friends and we almost made Teddy sit with us and eat because we felt so comfortable there! The whole employees and kitchen sang happy birthday to me and I cried. Not just from happiness but from relieve & joy that a place like this exists. We got to talk to the only Mr. Jaiden a little and listened to his love , passion and desire to grow his restaurants and his team and I have no doubt every single one of their dreams and aspirations will come true. \n\nLong story short, there are not enough stars to truly rate the magic of el toro so I hope anyone & everyone can experience their magic.\nAlso Michelin star…. Please come🤭🤩\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten June 10, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
